# Choragus audio capability grants (§9) — example.
#
# Maps an app's manifest app-id to the audio capabilities it holds. choragusd
# reads this and enforces it (default-deny: an app gets only what is listed; an
# unlisted app gets nothing). In production this file is populated by Portcullis
# from each app's manifest declarations PLUS the user's approval at the grant
# surface — it is not hand-edited on a real system; this example documents the
# format and the posture.
#
# Format: one app per line, `app-id  cap[,cap...]`. Capabilities:
#   audio          play to your own routed sink, see your own streams (the norm)
#   microphone     capture from a mic device                  (user-visible)
#   audio_monitor  tap the system output / another stream     (the audio
#                  screen-record — prominently surfaced, rarely granted)

org.atrium.player      audio
org.atrium.meet        audio,microphone
org.atrium.recorder    audio,audio_monitor
